      "answer": "The approved live patch window for Verdant Bay is on 2026-03-24 from 02:00 to 04:00 local time. If validation checks fail during the live patch, the rollback procedure is to run the command `orchestrator rollback --target ruleset=<prior_sha>`, which rehydrates the prior ruleset and replays the invalidation hook. After rollback, the steps include notifying Verdant Bay, opening an incident for manual remediation, and reverting any partial replays. These details come from the official Orchestrator emergency playbook and the renewal negotiation call with Verdant Bay, which confirm the timing and rollback process exactly as stated [art_fff67d92fe41], [art_f893faeda15a]. \n\nNo further detailed step-by-step rollback instructions beyond the CLI command and high-level post-rollback steps are provided in the evidence. Also, the evidence does not specify the exact validation check criteria beyond running validation jobs with synthetic and in-flight approvals during the patch window [art_fff67d92fe41].",
