      "answer": "Temporary field mappings planned in the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot router transform include mapping txn_id to transaction_id, total_amount to amount_cents, type coercion from string to int, preserving key fields store_id and register_id, and adding a transformation flag field _ns_transform=true. This transform is to be deployed in the SI-CLOUD-ROUTER component as a temporary measure to address SI-SCHEMA-REG rejections caused by mixed field names and types from store-level preprocessing. The transform will also enable OR-AUDIT-LOGS for each transformed event to ensure compliance and rollback safety [art_5a91258f4056].\n\nThe March 23 workshop in the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot is a Schema Signoff Workshop with the agenda to agree on a canonical schema for payment, register_events, and sensor_thermo events; define alias mapping; and plan producer migration. The deliverable from this workshop is a signed schema document to be uploaded to SI-SCHEMA-REG and a change control ticket with producer migration milestones. The workshop is scheduled for 90 minutes on 2026-03-23 and involves key stakeholders including Sophie Tremblay, Marc Gauthier, Ellen Park, Platform engineers, and Northstar SE/Ing teams [art_5a91258f4056].",
