      "answer": "The customer most likely to defect to a cheaper tactical competitor if the next promised milestone is missed is Pioneer Freight Solutions. They are currently running a tactical proof of concept (PoC) of NoiseGuard, a low-mid pricing tactical noise reduction competitor. The risk is that if Northstar misses acceptance milestones, Pioneer Freight's procurement is likely to extend NoiseGuard usage and reduce scope with Northstar, indicating a high retention risk [art_e2727db588de, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_7373b64fdfdd].\n\nThe exact milestone at risk is the acceptance milestone for the remediation plan addressing the taxonomy change incident at Pioneer Freight. This milestone includes achieving specific acceptance criteria during the validation window from May 1, 2026, to May 14, 2026. The acceptance criteria are:\n- precision@10 for facility lookups >= 0.8,\n- entity-link hit rate >= 90%,\n- grouping false positives <= 5%.\n\nFailure to meet this milestone by the agreed dates triggers a one-time credit of 10% of the Annual Contract Value ($42,000) and is linked to renewal redline negotiations [art_7373b64fdfdd, art_ac8afb52f2d3, art_79cf94421871].\n\nNo other customers are identified in the evidence as being at comparable risk of defecting to cheaper tactical competitors if milestones are missed, so Pioneer Freight Solutions is the most likely candidate based on the available information. Additional details on intermediate milestones or delivery dates beyond the validation window are not provided in the evidence [missing parts].",
